  "title": "Peer to Peer — Marisol/Daphne/Auriea",
  "summary": "Auriea Harvey, an artist and game designer, crafts digital figures based on her own scans, mythological characters, and art history. <em>Marisol/Daphne/Auriea</em> draws from the myth of Daphne, who was transformed into a laurel tree to escape Apollo. Harvey responds to the terror of this story with joy, depicting her figure dancing as it liquefies in color. This work also references a 1978 drawing by Pop artist Marisol, echoing its use of bodily outlines and a vibrant color palette. Harvey's figure, suspended between two and three dimensions, shifts in color and form with each reload, its ambiguous definition reflecting women's ongoing struggle for self-definition and transformation.",
